Description: avfilter/tonemapx: linearize Dolby Vision L'M'S' before the LMS to RGB matrix
 tonemapx converted Dolby Vision L'M'S' to R'G'B' by applying the LMS
 to RGB matrix to the PQ-coded values. The matrix is defined on linear
 light: the conversion is PQ EOTF, matrix, PQ OETF, as libplacebo and
 this tree's tonemap_cuda and tonemap_opencl do it. The comment on
 lms2rgb() named the shortcut: "This implementation does not do the
 costly linearization and de-linearization for performance reasons.
 The output color accuracy will be affected due to this".
 .
 The rows of the matrix sum to one, so a neutral pixel came out right
 and the error grew with saturation. Measured on flat synthetic patches
 of a profile 5 source with BT.2020 PQ output, a colour 90 base-layer
 codes from neutral came out 4 luma codes too high on average and up
 to 14, and colours 260 codes from neutral up to 119 too high. The
 conversion is shared by every output of the filter for the sources
 whose reshaping it applies, which are those with RPU profile 0 and no
 enhancement layer residual, profile 5 among them.
 .
 Apply the PQ EOTF to L'M'S', then the matrix, then the PQ OETF. Both
 curves are read from tables with linear interpolation: 16384 steps
 per unit of the signal for the EOTF, and 64 steps per octave of the
 linear value over 40 octaves for the OETF. The C, SSE4.2 and NEON
 paths share one scalar routine, and the AVX2 path gathers from the
 same tables.
 .
 The EOTF table runs to a signal of 1.375. L'M'S' of a bright saturated
 pixel is above 1, up to 1.36 with the profile 5 matrix, and clamping
 it to 1 before the matrix gives a different colour from the GPU
 filters, which do not clamp there. Linear RGB below zero comes out as
 zero on every path. The vector paths used to carry negative R'G'B'
 on, where the C path already clipped it.
